MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Stabbing the Drama feels like a natural next choice because I already listen to Figure Number Five and want more of Soilwork's combination of aggressive riffs and melodic hooks.",
    "Comalies appeals to my interest in heavy guitars paired with melodic vocals, which connects with what I enjoy in In Flames and Soilwork."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Scum offers heaviness, but its abrasive grindcore approach misses the melodic hooks I want today; Peeping Tom's experimental crossover is also less appealing than guitar-driven metal right now.",
    "Every Man For Himself connects with my history with The Reason, but I am choosing heavier music this visit. Night at the Opera leaves me unsure which album I would be choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Being heavy or aggressive seems to count too much when the balance between intensity and melody is what makes an album appealing to me today.",
    "My past interest in hard rock seems to be treated as enough reason to choose more of it now, even though those recommendations are secondary to the melodic metal choices on this page."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and my interest in Figure Number Five make the combination of melodic hooks and aggressive guitars especially relevant.",
    "I want momentum as well as heaviness right now: October Rust interests me, but a more driving album such as Stabbing the Drama is a stronger choice today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy guitar music, but only some capture the driving riffs and melodic hooks that make me want to choose an album today."
}
